# §1. The probability chain, checked

**§12 tail.** REG_r^c = {R(U) > (ε₀/r)^{1/5}}; a bounded-mean, bounded-covariance
8-dim Gaussian gives P(R > x) ≤ C e^{−cx²} by union bound, hence
P(REG_r^c) ≤ C_R exp(−c_R ε₀^{2/5} r^{−2/5}) — exponent arithmetic
((ε₀/r)^{1/5})² = ε₀^{2/5}r^{−2/5} ✓. Super-polynomial ✓, **conditional on the
uniform-law input imported from 044.**

**§13 determinant identities.** det H_M = f_xxf_yy − f_xy² = (rA_M)Q_M − (rB_M)²
= r[A_MQ_M − rB_M²] ✓ exact; W_r² ≤ r⁴(|A_MQ_M|+rB_M²)²(|A_SQ_S|+rB_S²)² is
degree-8 in V_r, so uniform eighth moments give E[W_r²] ≤ C_W r⁴ ✓.

**The Cauchy–Schwarz transfer — the step the whole tail section stands on:**

P_MS(E) = E[W_r 1_E]/Z_r ≤ √(E[W_r²] P(E))/Z_r ≤ (√C_W/c_Z)·√P(E),

because √(r⁴)/r² = 1: **the r-powers cancel exactly.** A Gaussian tail
exp(−c r^{−α}) transfers to a Palm tail exp(−(c/2)r^{−α}) with no power loss ✓.
This is the cleanest load-bearing line in §§12–14 and it is correct.

**§11 scale separation.** On REG_r, R⁴ ≤ (ε₀/r)^{4/5}, so
RW ≥ 1/(KR⁴) ≥ r^{4/5}/(Kε₀^{4/5}) and r/(RW) = O(r^{1/5}) ✓ — the exact-field
C¹ perturbation is asymptotically below every deterministic slack.

**§15 assembly.** The inclusion A_r^c ⊆ {s > −C_cap} ∪ REG_r^c ∪ {H₅ > r^{−1}}
is the contrapositive of Theorem 11.1 ✓ (deterministic side: CW's rederivation;
my own spot-checks of Lemmas 3.1, 4.1, 7.2, 7.3, 8.1, 8.3 all verify — μW = F*
