# §2. Lemma 13.1, strengthened: V_r is a linear pushforward

047 proves uniform moments for V_r via removable singularities in the confluent
frame. There is a shorter route that also removes a review surface entirely:

**V_r = L_r · (midpoint 15-jet), with L_r analytic in r.** Taylor at the
midpoint: f_xx(M) = f_xx(0) − (r/2)f_xxx(0) + (r²/8)f_xxxx(0) − …, and the exact
pins control f_xx(0), fix the f_xxx-combination, and leave the rest as the
sampled jets — so f_xx(M)/r is an **analytic-in-r linear functional of the
midpoint jets**, with coalesced limit −½f_xxx(0) → −1, matching J_M's entry
−1 + rc₄₀/12. Likewise f_xy(M)/r → −a/2 and f_yy(M) = q − (r/2)w + … . Since
GP-DER-034/044 already give uniform bounds for the midpoint law, **Lemma 13.1 is
a corollary of boundedness under analytic linear maps** — no separate
removable-singularity argument is needed, and one fewer place for a reviewer to
worry. Offered as replacement text on request.

